      "content": "that's exactly what i was looking for. it makes the whole debate feel much more grounded in reality. one thing though, i've seen some people arguing that we should instead focus on things like job retraining or tax incentives for companies that keep humans on staff. in my article, i want to address these, but i don't want to give them too much credit if they're fundamentally flawed. how would you characterize those opposing views in a way that shows they're just outdated or unrealistic given the scale of what ai is doing?",
